00:32:52.840 --> 00:32:53.500
is created.

00:32:53.500 --> 00:32:56.530
I'll keep these as default
for now and click Create.

00:33:00.540 --> 00:33:01.700
Cool.

00:33:01.700 --> 00:33:03.537
So we have created a KMS key.

00:33:03.537 --> 00:33:05.120
So next, we're going
to create our GCS

00:33:05.120 --> 00:33:07.520
bucket using this key for a
customer-managed encryption

00:33:07.520 --> 00:33:08.570
key.

00:33:08.570 --> 00:33:11.670
So let's go over to the
Google Cloud Storage browser.

00:33:11.670 --> 00:33:12.680
Click Create Bucket.

00:33:12.680 --> 00:33:15.230
So I'm going to follow
a similar pattern--

00:33:15.230 --> 00:33:18.250
"credit-card-support-team-logs."

00:33:18.250 --> 00:33:20.750
And I'm going to select
